  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/langs2/). VERDICT: CURRENT. 2026-11-01 review at dev 100b6fbb6e: analyze_java on the filed A/B fixture emits A.m -> A.m (ast_call_direct); java.py L3021 still routes object_node 'super' through Case 1 (gikuk 495f9747f5 made the lookup positional, behaviour unchanged). In survey output the self-loop is removed by deduplicate_edges(remove_self_loops=True), which is why WI-latin saw no edge. A visible false edge exists too: super.go() inside a NON-override Kid.other binds Kid.other -> Kid.go instead of Base.go; super.write(b) on external OutputStream also self-loops. MECHANISM: java Case 1 treats super like this: looks up <EnclosingClass>.m, so super.m() binds the subclass's own m. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-latin."  # 6cd5
